                      "quoteExcerpt": "\u003creferencable-result>\\nID: 9\\n\",\n      \"type\": \"input_text\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"标题: Nexstar rides record political spending to 13.3% gain in Q3 revenue | S&P Global Market Intelligence\\n溯源地址: https://www.spglobal.com/marketintelligence/en/news-insights/trending/75nqdgtxqzf_qhv5k_f5rw2\\n发布时间: 2018-11-08 14:02:00\\n摘要: Nexstar rides record political spending to 13.3% gain in Q3 revenue\\nTheme Technology, Media & Telecom\\nContinuing the strong results among station operators, Nexstar Media Group Inc. registered record political advertising with the 2018 midterm election cycle.\\nThe nation's No. 2 station operator said political ad spending reached the high end of its revised guidance with gross bookings expected to range between a record $280 million and $290 million for the year, which will result in net political ad revenue of $245 million.\\nDuring the third quarter alone, Nexstar registered a record $70.2 million in political ad revenue, an almost tenfold jump from $7.2 million in the third quarter of 2017.\\nThe company said its broadcast and digital solutions were used by federal level candidates across a wide swath of its footprint, with heavy spending in West Virginia, In\n\n[……中间省略 2400 字符……]\n\nre upside, which the medium evidently realized.\\n\\\"The numbers speak for themselves. TV remains at the forefront of ad choices for political decision-makers,\\\" Passwaiter said in a release. Kantar had pegged political ad spending on local stations at $2.10 billion for the 2014 midterms.\\nThere was strong spending behind a number of key U.S. Senate races, as more than $115.5 million was allocated i",
